      <data key="d7">2022</data>
      <data key="d8">Machine learning (ML) prediction models have been applied to predict ARGs in beach waters.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gradient Boosted Regression Tree" target="Machine learning models" id="1">
      <data key="d4">EXTENDS</data>
      <data key="d5">0.6</data>
      <data key="d6">0388512f55246b6fd2347a5967c08fd4916b8540</data>
      <data key="d7">2022</data>
      <data key="d8">In this study, we developed a gradient boosted regression tree based (GBRT) ML model</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gradient Boosted Regression Tree" target="Explainable AI" id="0">
      <data key="d4">USES</data>
      <data key="d5">0.8</data>
      <data key="d6">0388512f55246b6fd2347a5967c08fd4916b8540</data>
      <data key="d7">2022</data>
      <data key="d8">In this study, we developed a gradient boosted regression tree based (GBRT) ML model and then described its behavior using six explainable artificial intelligence (XAI) model-agnostic explanation methods.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gradient Boosted Regression Tree" target="Predictive models" id="0">
      <data key="d4">PRODUCES</data>
      <data key="d5">0.9</data>
      <data key="d6">0388512f55246b6fd2347a5967c08fd4916b8540</data>
      <data key="d7">2022</data>
      <data key="d8">We developed ML prediction models for aac (6'-lb-cr), sul1, and tetX with 10-fold time-blocked cross-validation performances of 4.9, 2.06 and 4.4 root mean squared logarithmic error, respectively.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gradient Boosted Regression Tree" target="hydro-meteorological and qPCR data" id="0">
      <data key="d4">EVALUATES_ON</data>
